{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And He overturned the cities.</b> From here it is implied that the overturning of Sodom preceded the death of Sarah, but in the passage of the [ Levirate widow's] shoe [in the Talmud] the opposite is implied, as it was taught there: Eliezer the servant of Abraham happened to arrive at the place of Sodom, and they sought to bring him to the bed [for levirate relations]. He said to them: from the day of Sarah's death I have not ascended to the bed — thus it implies that the death of Sarah preceded. Rather, one may answer: that which was taught, 'Eliezer happened to arrive at the place of Sodom' — that is Zoar, and Zoar was not overturned." "<b>And the soil's produce.</b> Rabbi Yehoshua ben Levi said: now let a person gather soil from the earth of Sodom and place it in another furrow — it does not grow."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:58.106162369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}